  "cli_result_text": "Files submitted. Summary of the traced boundary:\n\n**Flow:** `fastapi/dependencies/utils.py::solve_dependencies` \u2192 `request_body_to_args` (line ~430) calls `field.validate(value, ...)` on each `ModelField` in `dependant.body_params`. In `fastapi/_compat.py`, the Pydantic-v2 `ModelField.validate` (dataclass defined for `PYDANTIC_V2`) delegates to `self._type_adapter.validate_python(value, from_attributes=True)`, a `pydantic.TypeAdapter` built over `Annotated[field_info.annotation, field_info]` \u2014 this is the FastAPI\u2192Pydantic-v2 crossing point, and it's where a `ValidationError` would normally get converted into the 422 response; if no error is raised here, none is ever surfaced.\n\n**Root cause boundary:** Pydantic's schema builder wraps a model's `model_validator(mode='before')` **around** (outside) the `model-fields` core schema via `apply_model_validators(schema, model_validators, 'outer')` in `pydantic/_internal/_generate_schema.py`. A `mode='before'` validator therefore runs on the raw input dict *before* pydantic-core evaluates any nested field, including a discriminated-union field. The discriminator resolution itself lives in `pydantic/_internal/_discriminated_union.py`'s `_ApplyInferredDiscriminator`, which converts the `Union[...]` into a `tagged-union` core schema keyed off the discriminator field's `Literal` value \u2014 but that tagged-union validator only ever sees whatever dict the outer `function-before` step handed it.\n\n**Why it fails silently:** if the customer's `model_validator(mode='before')` reshapes/filters the incoming JSON (e.g., renaming keys, dropping \"unrecognized\" keys, or restructuring a nested payload) and in doing so drops the discriminator key \u2014 or drops the entire union field's key \u2014 pydantic-core never reaches the `tagged-union` discriminator-mismatch error path at all. If the field itself is `Optional`/has a default, a missing key is legal and pydantic-core just substitutes the default (`None`) rather than raising `union_tag_invalid` or `missing`. No exception propagates back through `TypeAdapter.validate_python` \u2192 `ModelField.validate` \u2192 `request_body_to_args`, so FastAPI's error-collection path in `solve_dependencies`/`request_body_to_args` never populates `errors`, and the route handler is invoked with the field silently `None` \u2014 hence 200 OK with a dropped field instead of 422.",
  "cli_is_error": false,
